# The natural spelling of "enum with default" -- and, since 2026-08-26
# (the preference admission gate, ADR-004), the WORKING one: an
# override must be admitted by an alternative or equal the preferred
# value, so "superadmin" is refused with [aontu/empty] (asserted by
# check.sh). Unset, the field generates "member". Vet also reports a
# pref_not_instance advisory: the default is a member of the admitted
# set only by being the default -- repeat the branch (see
# enum-default-repeated.aon) to state it as a first-class member.
invite: role: *member | admin | owner
